.TH "awww\-restore" "1" "2026\-07\-19"
.PP
.SH NAME
awww\-restore
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBawww restore\fR
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fB\-a\fR,\fB\-\-all\fR
.RS 4
Send this command to all active \fBawww\-daemon\fR namespaces.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-n\fR,\fB\-\-namespace\fR <namespace>
.RS 4
Which wayland namespace to send this command to.\&
.PP
You can specify this option multiple times to send commands to multiple
namespaces at once: \fBawww restore \-n <namespace1> \-n <namespace 2>\fR.\&
.PP
This affects the name of the \fBawww\-daemon\fR socket we will use to
communicate with.\& Specifically, our socket name is
\fI${WAYLAND_DISPLAY}\-awww\-daemon.\&<specified namespace>.\&socket\fR.\&
.PP
Some compositors can have several different wallpapers per output.\& This
allows you to differentiate between them.\& Most users will probably not have
to set anything in this option.\&
.PP
.PP
.RE
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-outputs\fR
.RS 4
Comma separated list of outputs to restore.\& Use \fBawww query\fR to know which
outputs are currently being used.\&
.PP
If it isn'\&t set, all outputs will be restored.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.RS 4
Print help (see a summary with '\&\-h'\&)
.PP
.RE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Restores the last displayed image on the specified outputs.\&
.PP
This can be used to split initialization (with \fBawww init \-\-no\-daemon\fR) and
cache loading into different steps, in order to avoid race condition traps.\&
.PP
You can also use this command to restore the last displayed image when
reconnecting a monitor.\&
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBawww\-clear\-cache\fR(1)
